- op: create  # 18af
  at: '2026-08-24T21:02:52Z'  # 18af
  by: agent  # 18af
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 18af
  clock: 1  # 18af
  nonce: 18af  # 18af
  data:  # 18af
    kind: invariant  # 18af
    title: "Symbol-id slot parsing has no gate: ~15 positional parses remain, collapsing 80 objc entities into 17 and silently disabling the id validators"  # 18af
    status: violated  # 18af
    priority: 1  # 18af
    parent:  # 18af
    tags:  # 18af
    - identifier_format  # 18af
    - analysis_quality  # 18af
    - objc  # 18af
    - node_identity  # 18af
    isbefore: []  # 18af
    duplicate_of: []  # 18af
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 18af
    pr_ref:  # 18af
    description: "FOUND 2026-08-24 while diagnosing WI-nakut. WI-nakut's symptom (an empty method\nname in a caveat) is one visible tip of this; the class is much larger and the\ndamage is node identity, linker recovery, and the ID VALIDATORS THEMSELVES.\n\nTHE GRAMMAR. Per ADR-0036 (D1a) the PATH slot is colon-tolerant, and in\npractice so is the NAME slot (objc selectors, rust `Error::new`). Measured\nagainst real production ids, ONLY TWO positional accesses are safe:\n\n    parts[0]   language   colon-free by grammar   SAFE\n    parts[-1]  kind       colon-free by grammar   SAFE\n\nEvery other positional access is WRONG on at least one real id shape:\n\n  objc:external:0-0:writeToFile:atomically::unresolved\n     parts[-2] = ''              symbol_name_slot = 'writeToFile:atomically:'\n     parts[3]  = 'writeToFile'   (truncated)\n     parts[-3] = 'atomically'    (NOT the span)\n  rust:std::io:0-0:Error::new:external_symbol\n     parts[1]  = 'std'           symbol_path_slot = 'std::io'\n     parts[-2] = 'new'           symbol_name_slot = 'Error::new'\n     parts[-3] = ''              (NOT the span)\n  dart:dart:io:0-0:module:module\n     parts[1]  = 'dart'          symbol_path_slot = 'dart:io'\n\nINV-fokik ALREADY BUILT THE CHOKEPOINTS AND DID NOT BUILD A GATE.\nsymbol_path_slot / symbol_name_slot are span-anchored and correct, and\n_parse_dangling_id's docstring says \"this function was one of the two homes\nthat already had it right, and it is now one of four that share it\". Four were\nconverted. Nothing prevents a fifth, and there are now ~15.\n\nA NARROWED SCAN (split of an id-ish variable, then a positional index) finds\n32 sites; excluding the two grammar-safe slots leaves roughly 15 live defects\nacross core, linkers, validators and the CLI. Notable ones:\n\n  ir.py:1523                 parts[-2] -> the DEDUPE KEY for boundary nodes\n  ir.py:1520                 parts[-2] (the <5-part fallback)\n  linkers/method_call_recovery.py:117   parts[-2] on an :unresolved dst\n  linkers/napi.py:265, pyffi.py:449, lua_ffi.py:245   same shape\n  verify_claims.py:1372,2019,2481,2576,2607   parts[1] / parts[3]\n  io_boundary.py:3045        parts[1]\n  profile.py:3359,3366       parts[1]\n  spec_validator.py:1759-61  parts[-3]/[-2]/[-1]\n  cli.py:5400                parts[-2] (display label)\n\nMEASURED DAMAGE, THREE KINDS.\n\n(1) NODE IDENTITY. ir.py:1523 feeds _dedupe_key(language, path, name), so an\nempty name collapses distinct entities into ONE node. On Mantle (31 .m files,\nreal upstream repo):\n      external dsts                                  319 (94 distinct)\n      dsts whose parsed name is EMPTY                268   (84%)\n      distinct names via symbol_name_slot             80\n      distinct names via parts[-2]                    17   (79% LOST)\n      one node `objc:external:0-0::external_symbol` absorbs 49 edges /\n      134 distinct call sites (meta.call_lines)\n      id_format violations reported                   71\n\n(2) LINKER RECOVERY. method_call_recovery / napi / pyffi / lua_ffi each take\nparts[-2] off an `:unresolved` dst, so every multi-part objc selector gives\nthem an empty name and those edges cannot be recovered at all. NOT separately\nquantified.\n\n(3) THE VALIDATORS ARE SILENTLY DEAD ON COLON-BEARING IDS -- the worst of the\nthree, because it is the check that exists to catch producer derivation bugs.\nvalidate_symbol_id_format locates the span at parts[-3] and returns None early\nwhen it is not \"0-0\". Same WI-davan defect, three languages:\n\n    python:packages.foo.src.bar:0-0:x:external_symbol          -> CAUGHT\n    objc:packages.foo.src.bar:0-0:writeToFile:atomically::...  -> None\n    rust:packages.foo.src.bar:0-0:Error::new:external_symbol   -> None\n\nspec_validator.py:1758-1761 uses the same parse.\n\nWHY OBJECTIVE-C IS CATASTROPHIC AND RUST IS ONLY LOSSY. A selector ENDS with a\ncolon, so parts[-2] is the EMPTY STRING rather than a truncation. An empty name\nis a dedupe-key COLLISION, not merely a bad label. Rust's `Error::new` -> `new`\nis a truncation: measured on bellman, 1 truncating node and 0 colliding keys.\n\nNOT CAUSED BY INV-rilit (PR #510), CHECKED. That change puts `::` into rust\nmodule_attr_ref ids, so it looked like it might widen this. It does not:\nboundary-node materialization SPLITS the qualified name\n(`rust:std::env::consts:0-0:OS:external_symbol`), leaving the name slot\ncolon-free. bellman shows 1 truncating node and 0 colliding keys BOTH before\nand after.\n\nTHE FIX HAS RULE-7 SHAPE: not \"fix ir.py:1523\" but route the remaining sites\nthrough the existing chokepoints AND ADD A GATE (the\ncheck-multi-value-field-axis-declaration family) that fails on a new positional\nparse of a symbol id. A shrink-only baseline, as the mypy ratchet uses, is the\nobvious vehicle for the ~15 existing sites. Without the gate this recurs; it\nalready has, five times.\n\nNOT MEASURED: how many repos in the corpus contain objc at all; whether swift\nor any other language carries colon-bearing names; the linker-recovery loss in\n(2); whether any currently-shipped verdict depends on a collapsed node."  # 18af
    fields:  # 18af
      statement: "Every read of a symbol-id slot must go through the span-anchored chokepoints (ir.symbol_path_slot / ir.symbol_name_slot), and a gate must make that enforceable rather than aspirational. Only parts[0] (language) and parts[-1] (kind) are colon-free by the grammar; any other positional access is wrong on a real production id, and the failures are silent -- a collapsed node, an unrecoverable linker edge, or a validator that returns None instead of reporting the defect it exists to catch."  # 18af
      root_cause: "INV-fokik created symbol_path_slot and symbol_name_slot and converted four call sites, but added no gate, so the doctrine leaked. _parse_dangling_id is the clearest case: it routes the PATH half to the chokepoint and hand-rolls the NAME as parts[-2], while its own docstring claims it 'already had it right'. Objective-C selectors END with a colon, so parts[-2] is the empty string rather than a truncation, and an empty name is a dedupe-key collision rather than a bad label."  # 18af
