- op: discuss  # 1c91
  at: '2026-08-25T02:55:57Z'  # 1c91
  by: agent  # 1c91
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1c91
  clock: 7  # 1c91
  nonce: 1c91  # 1c91
  message: "STATUS -> SATISFIED 2026-08-24. CORRECTING MYSELF: I left this violated after\nPR #515 on the grounds that \"the remaining half\" -- producer-side sanitisation\nin make_unresolved_edge, so Edge.dst stops carrying the raw selector -- was\nstill outstanding. THAT WAS NOT THIS ITEM'S STATEMENT AND IT HAS NO MEASURED\nHARM TODAY. Keeping a fixed item open on an invented residual is the same\nstale-status failure I closed INV-funam and INV-rilit for in this same session.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on the merged tree (dev @f21a8e67ba, PR #515), Mantle --\nthis item's OWN measured population, re-run:\n\n                                    FILED      NOW\n  distinct selectors                80 -> 17   19 -> 82 (scored both ways,\n                                               ONE survey, instrument compare)\n  dsts whose parsed name is EMPTY   268/319    0\n  boundary nodes with name=''       (the       0\n                                    collapse)\n  one node absorbing 49 edges /\n    134 call sites                  yes        gone (identity is the lossless\n                                               name, so the merge cannot form)\n  id_format violations              71         115 -> 44, and ZERO of the 44\n                                               are on an objc external\n                                               selector node\n\nPublished CLI, the layer a reader sees:\n  \"distinct method(s): .\"  ->  \"distinct method(s): writeToFile:atomically:\"\n\nTHE 44 REMAINING id_format VIOLATIONS ARE A DIFFERENT DEFECT and are not this\nitem's: every one is non_canonical_language_prefix -- a HEADER PATH in the LANG\nslot (Foundation/Foundation.h:<unknown>:0-0:...:external_symbol, language=null),\na different producer. Recorded on INV-dulah, the standing umbrella for\n\"node.id format escapes documented grammar\". Naming it here so the closure is\nnot read as \"id_format is clean on Mantle\" -- it is not.\n\nON THIS ITEM'S OWN STATEMENT, which is the thing a closure is judged against:\nit is REFUTED and was refuted by the suite earlier in this session\n(test_id_format_validator_names_the_name_slot_colon_not_the_span). The statement\nasserts \"Only parts[0] and parts[-1] are colon-free by the grammar; any other\npositional access is wrong\". ADR-0036 Ruling 1 makes the NAME slot colon-free BY\nRULE via sanitize_id_name_segment, so parts[-2] is CORRECT on a well-formed id\nand the ~15 \"defects\" I counted were the grammar being relied on. The real\ndefect was never a parsing one: Ruling 1's designated lossless home\n(Symbol.name) was NEVER FILLED, which made the id the name's only home -- the\none arrangement the ruling forbids. That is what #515 fixed.\n\nWHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT CLAIMED. Edge.dst still carries the raw selector\n(objc:external:0-0:writeToFile:atomically::unresolved). That is ADR-0036's OWN\ndeferred follow-up, recorded in its id-format:F3 amendment, not this item's\nstatement -- and it causes no measured harm now: Edge.dst is not a Symbol.id so\nthe validator does not check it, and every consumer reads the lossless home\ninstead of parsing it. It is safe to do NOW and was not before #515 (folding\nfirst would have destroyed the name the lossless home preserves). If it is\nwanted, it wants its own item against ADR-0036's amendment, not this one held\nopen as a placeholder.\n\nAlso not claimed: NO VERDICT FLIPPED. This is identity and disclosure quality,\nnot coverage. And only objc and rust were measured at population level -- the\nproducer change is central so it reaches all 36 analyzers, but the effect on the\nother 34 is UNMEASURED.\n\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/divuf_fix_08242026/README.md"  # 1c91
- op: discuss  # b0a1
  at: '2026-08-25T03:03:12Z'  # b0a1
  by: agent  # b0a1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b0a1
  clock: 8  # b0a1
  nonce: b0a1  # b0a1
  message: "CORRECTION TO MY OWN CLOSURE EVIDENCE 2026-08-24, prompted by being asked\nwhether I was certain. THE CLOSURE STANDS; TWO OF THE NUMBERS IN IT DO NOT.\nBoth errors ran in the flattering direction (they overstated the delta), so\nthey are corrected here rather than left.\n\nWHAT I WROTE, AND WHY IT WAS WRONG:\n\n1. \"distinct selectors 19 -> 82\" was presented as a before/after. IT IS NOT.\n   The 19 came from an INTERMEDIATE cache built with my OWN id regression in it\n   (the first cut, which pushed raw colons into the minted boundary id). It is\n   not the pre-fix state of dev. Re-measured on the merged tree, the SAME\n   parts[-2] read now yields 82 distinct and 0 empty -- because edge dsts are\n   remapped to the canonical boundary id and that id is now well-formed, so a\n   positional read is CORRECT on it. That is Ruling 1's own claim demonstrated,\n   not a defect; but it means the \"19\" arm never existed on shipped dev.\n\n2. \"id_format 115 -> 44\" has the same flaw. The 115 was the intermediate state\n   carrying my regression. This item's FILED pre-fix figure is 71. So the\n   defensible statement is: filed 71, merged tree measures 44.\n\nWHAT IS ACTUALLY MEASURED ON THE MERGED TREE (dev @83f9cae52a), and is what the\nclosure rests on:\n\n  Mantle, objc external boundary nodes\n    nodes                         59\n    nodes with an EMPTY name       0\n    DISTINCT names                59      (1:1 -- no collapse survives)\n    ids with a colon in the name   0\n    id_format violations          44, and ZERO on a selector node; every one is\n                                  non_canonical_language_prefix (the lang-slot\n                                  limb recorded on INV-dulah)\n\n  Repro CLI, this item's user-facing symptom\n    \"distinct method(s): .\"  ->  \"distinct method(s): writeToFile:atomically:\"\n\n  bellman -- the only TRUE paired pre/post across the change\n    id_format violations           1 -> 0\n    truncated boundary nodes      13 -> 16 qualified (batch_normalize splits\n                                  back into E::G1:: and E::G2::)\n    nodes/edges                   862/2467 -> 865/2470\n    cross_field                  119 -> 119, verdicts unchanged\n\nWHY THE CLOSURE STILL STANDS. The item's filed damage was a COLLAPSE: 268 of\n319 dsts nameless, 80 distinct selectors rendered as 17, one node absorbing 49\nedges from 134 call sites. On the merged tree Mantle has 59 external nodes with\n59 distinct names and zero empty ones -- the collapse cannot form, because\nidentity is now the lossless name. That is a direct measurement of the filed\ndefect's absence, not an inference from a delta.\n\nWHAT I STILL CANNOT CLAIM: there is no pre-fix Mantle survey in hand, so\nnothing here is a clean paired before/after ON THAT REPO -- the pre-fix column\nis the item's own filed figures (319 dsts / 94 distinct / 268 nameless), and\nthe post-fix population is 229 external-bearing dsts. DIFFERENT POPULATIONS,\nso the pair is indicative, not arithmetic. bellman is the only genuine pair."  # b0a1
